  "_comment": "The cut, as data. Shots are contiguous hard cuts on the music's beat grid (src/data/beat-grid.json, 100 BPM = 600 ms a beat, 4 beats a bar); shot i ends where shot i+1 starts. Anchors resolve through src/timeline/resolve.mjs, which the gate imports too. Never type startMs by hand; use an anchor. Bars fall on beat indices 4k; act changes sit on bars, voice-led cuts may sit on the half-bar. narration.offsetMs places the Eva take so cue a2 (the seat price) ends just before KILLED and c1 (\"Rebuilt on Monid\") starts over the stamp. Text here is data-free: every figure on screen is read from results/ or external-facts.json by the component that draws it. Act A opens with a photo burst: six tight crops of the tracked Brand24 captures at one beat each, `flash: true` (one-frame plate flash, shutter). `sfx.volume` is the bus for every synthesised effect under public/sfx/.",
